{
  "title": "Dua for Solving Difficulties",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِیْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nیَا عِمَادَ مَنْ لَا عِمَادَ لَہٗ\nYAA E'MAADA MAN LAA E'MAADA LAHU\nO Support of him who lacks support!\nوَ یَا ذُخْرَ مَنْ لَا ذُخْرَ لَہٗ\nWA YAA ZUKHRA MAN LAA ZUKHRA LAHU\nO Hoard of him who lacks hoard!\nوَ یَا سَنَدَ مَنْ لَا سَنَدَ لَہٗ\nWA YAA SANADA MAN LAA SANADA LAHU\nO Prop of him who lacks prop!\nوَ یَا حِرْزَ مَنْ لَا حِرْزَ لَہٗ\nWA YAA HIRZA MAN LAA HIRZA LAHU\nO Shelter of him who lacks shelter!\nوَ یَا غِیَاثَ مَنْ لَا غِیَاثَ لَہٗ\nWA YAA GHEYAASA MAN LAA GHEYAASA LAHU\nO Aid of him who is aidless!\nوَ یَا كَنْزَ مَنْ لَا كَنْزَ لَہٗ\nWA YAA KANZA MAN LAA KANZA LAHU\nO Treasure of him who has no treasure!\nوَ یَا عِزَّ مَنْ لَا عِزَّ لَہٗ\nWA YAA I'ZZA MAN LAA I'ZZA LAHU\nO Might of him who wants might!\nیَا كَرِیْمَ الْعَفْوِ\nYAA KAREEMAL A'FWE\nO He Who pardons generously!\nیَا حَسَنَ التَّجَاوُزِ\nYAA HASANAT TAJAA-WOZE\nO He Who overlooks excellently!\nیَا عَوْنَ الضُّعَفَاۤءِ\nYAA A'WNAZ ZO-A'FAA-E\nO Helper of the weak!\nیَا كَنْزَ الْفُقَرَاۤءِ\nYAA KANZAL FOQARAA-E\nO Treasure of the poor!\nیَا عَظِیْمَ الرَّجَاۤءِ\nYAA A'ZEEMAR RAJAA-E\nO He Who is greatly hoped!\nیَا مُنْقِذَ الْغَرْقیٰ\nYAA MUNQEZAL GHARQAA\nO Savior of the drowned!\nیَا مُنْجِیَ الْھَلْكیٰ\nYAA MUNJEYAL HALKAA\nO Rescuer of the perishing!\nیَا مُحْسِنُ یَا مُجْمِلُ یَا مُنْعِمُ یَا مُفْضِلُ\nYAA MOHSENO YAA MUJMELO YAA MUN-E'MO YAA MUFZELO\nO All-munificent! O All-benign! O All-gracious! O All-benevolent!\nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ سَجَدَ لَكَ سَوَادُ اللَّیْلِ وَ نُوْرُ النَّھَارِ وَ ضَوْءِ الْقَمَرِ وَ شُعَاعُ الشَّمْسِ وَ خَفِیْفُ الشَّجَرِ وَ دَوِیُّ الْمَاۤءِ\nANTAL LAZEE SAJADA LAKA SAWAADUL LAYLE WA NOORUN NAHAARE WA ZAW-UL QAMARE WA SHO-A'A-O'SH SHAMSE WA KHAFEEFUSH SHAJARE WA DAWIYYUL MAA-E\nIt is You alone before Whom the darkness of night has prostrated, as have the light of day, the brightness of the moon, the radiance of the sun, the rustle of trees, and the murmur of water.\nیَاۤ اَللّٰهُ یَاۤ اَللّٰهُ یَاۤ اَللّٰهُ\nYAA ALLAAHO, YAA ALLAAHO, YAA ALLAAHO\nO Allah! O Allah! O Allah!\nلَاۤ اِلٰہَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ وَحْدَكَ لَا شَرِیْكَ لَكَ\nLAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA, WAHDAKA LAA SHAREEKA LAKA\nThere is no god save You; You are the One and Only without having any partner.\nیَا رَبَّاہُ یَاۤ اَللّٰهُ\nYAA RABBAAHO YAA ALLAAHO\nO my Lord! O Allah!\nصَلِّ عَلٰی مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَ افْعَلْ بِنَا مَاۤ اَنْتَ اَھْلُہٗ\nSALLE A'LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN, WAF-A'L BENAA MAA ANTA AHLOHU\n(Please do) bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad and do to us all that which suits You.\n\nAfter this, ask for your legitimate desires.",
  "merits": "Shaykh Kaf'ami, in his book Baladul Ameen, has narrated this dua from Ameer al-Momineen, Imam Ali (a.s.). Whenever a person in difficult circumstances recites it, the Almighty solves his problems."
}
